# Student App Firebase Functions — Sync Update

**Send this to the student app team along with the updated [firebase-functions/index.js](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/firebase-functions/index.js).**

---

## What Changed & Why

We audited the admin and student app codebases and found the student app's [firebase-functions/index.js](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/firebase-functions/index.js) was out of date. Here's a summary of every change made to the file:

### ✅ Kept As-Is (Student App–Specific)
| Function | Reason |
|---|---|
| `validateUserDevice` | Student app uses exact device ID string match — correct for student flow |
| `registerUserDevice` | Student-specific implementation — correct as-is |
| `cleanupInvalidTokens` | Unchanged |

---

### 🔴 Critical Fix: Wrong Field Name in `notifyCourseUpdate`

**Before (WRONG):**
```js
.where("enrolledCourses", "array-contains", courseId)
```

**After (CORRECT):**
```js
.where("assignedCourseIds", "array-contains", courseId)
```

The user documents use `assignedCourseIds` — `enrolledCourses` doesn't exist. This meant **no course-update notifications were being triggered**.

---

### 🔴 Critical Fix: `notifyContentUpdate` Now Includes `itemIds`

The student app's badge system ([content_update_service.dart](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/lib/services/content_update_service.dart)) requires content update docs to include an `itemIds` array inside `contentChanges` so it can track which individual content items a student has seen. Without this, content-type "NEW" badges could never be cleared per individual item.

Each update doc now has:
```js
{
  type: "content_pdfs_updated",
  contentType: "pdfs",
  changeType: "added",
  itemIds: ["<id1>", "<id2>"],        // top-level (for direct access)
  contentChanges: [{                   // nested (for per-item tracking)
    type: "pdfs",
    change: "added",
    count: 2,
    itemIds: ["<id1>", "<id2>"]
  }],
  ...
}
```

---

### 🟡 Updated: `notifyModuleUpdate`

- Fixed to use `assignedCourseIds`
- Added `courseName` and `moduleName` to update docs (needed for UI)
- Sends FCM push via the shared [sendFcmToUsers](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/firebase-functions/index.js#299-334) helper

---

### 🟢 Added: `notifyContentItemUpdate` (NEW)

Tracks item-level changes within a module. Required for granular "NEW" badge tracking in the student app:
- Item title renamed → recorded (no push)
- Item description changed → recorded (no push)
- Item URL/content replaced → push sent
- Item published/unpublished → push sent

This function was completely missing from the old file.

---

### 🟢 Added: [getUnseenUpdatesCount](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/lib/services/content_update_service.dart#271-292) (NEW)

Callable function the student app uses to get the total unseen update count for the current user. Was missing from the old file.

---

### 🟢 Improved: `markUpdateAsSeen`

Now uses `HttpsError` consistently for permission errors.

---

### 🟢 Added: [sendFcmToUsers](file:///Users/rojinroy/Projects/briffiniApp/briffiniApp/firebase-functions/index.js#299-334) helper

Shared internal helper. Queries `user_tokens` where `appType == "student"` and `isActive == true`, then sends via `sendEachForMulticast`.

---

## Do NOT Deploy These From This Repo

The admin app deploys these separately — adding them here will cause conflicts:

- `sendChatNotification`, `sendCommunityNotification`, `sendPushNotification`
- `sendCourseAssignmentNotification`, `triggerConsolidatedCourseAssignmentNotification`
- `checkExpiringSubscriptions`, `markExpiredSubscriptions`
- `checkViolationResetStatus`, `recordScreenshotViolation`, `acknowledgeViolationReset`
- `toggleDeviceRestriction`, `resetUserDevice`, `getDeviceRestrictionStatus`
- `setCustomClaims`, `createUser`, `deleteUser`
- `subscribeToTopic`, `unsubscribeFromTopic`

---

## Deployment

```bash
cd firebase-functions
npm install
firebase deploy --only functions
```
